From f8d5675fb01f0d52da8f840489121d593a67e39d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:25:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] update pause requeue: a stopped head's cancel that
 committed before raising settles; document the post-commit Stop window

t_01a1d4cc43b7ac4a, the three non-blocking points of review 5890626978 of PR #2173, redone against main after
#2173 landed as 129a8e34216 (its first commit was superseded by ea4f9dc74e5, so the names moved).

1. `_stopped_after_requeue` cancel-failure path. On main the comment already states the real behaviour (the row
   stays queued and runs once after the hold) and no `cancel_obligations` entry exists any more, so nothing leaks.
   Decision: no retry loop. `db._execute_write` already retries a locked/busy writer within its write patience, so
   what reaches the handler is not transient, or its commit is unknown (an IOERR at COMMIT). For that last case the
   handler now reads the row back: a cancel that committed settles as cancelled (waiter answered, media released)
   instead of leaving the waiter hanging on a terminal row. Otherwise it logs ERROR that the row stays queued.
   New test, parametrized: before-commit (row queued, latch cleared, waiter unanswered, one attempt, the notice runs
   exactly once after the hold) and commit-then-raise (settled cancelled, waiter answered, never runs again).
2. `requeue_unstarted` docstring documents the one Stop window left, between the write's commit and the coroutine
   resuming: `interrupt_update` then reads the row queued and returns False, so its caller is told the turn does not
   stop and the notice runs once after the hold. No await separates the `stopped` read from clearing the claim.
3. Superseded: tests/gateway/test_update_pause_started_notifier_head.py never reached main. Main's bound-steer test
   (tests/gateway/test_update_hold_claimed_wake.py::test_a_steer_committed_while_the_wake_waited_on_the_lease_goes_back_with_it,
   d495dccb3fe) already drives the real `prompt.steer_queued` RPC into a BufferedAgent; it fakes no `_transfers`.

Tests: tests/gateway/test_update_requeue_stop_race.py: commit-then-raise is RED on origin/main's
session_update_pause.py (waiter never answered) and GREEN here; before-commit passes on both (characterizes
main's behaviour); 3 passed. The 21 test files that import session_update_pause / requeue_unstarted: 152 passed. scripts/check --base origin/main: ok.
---
 gateway/session_update_pause.py               | 26 +++++--
 .../gateway/test_update_requeue_stop_race.py  | 74 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 94 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

